{
  "about": "How the guided tasting fields, the precise score and the wine details are read: every implementation normalizes them the same way when it reads a record (docs/SYNC.md §1). Each 'input' is read inside a cellar (CaveKit's decoder, the Kotlin core's Cellar) and written back; the record must then equal 'read' (numbers compared by value). 'oldVersion' holds records with every new key, read by a decoder that knows only the keys of the previous version (RatingScaleVectorTests / TastingSheetTests on both platforms): it must keep them, and an edit it makes ('edit') must read back as 'afterEdit' in the new version. Dates are seconds since 2001-01-01.",
